      en: "The Amman Municipal Building serves as the administrative hub of Jordan's capital. Completed in 1955, it was designed by the British architect Austen Harrison. The building's design integrates modernist principles with local stonework, reflecting the city's post-independence development. It houses the offices of the mayor and city council, and its central location makes it a landmark for navigation. The building's square has hosted numerous protests and celebrations. The construction cost approximately 2 million Jordanian dinars. The clock tower stands at 50 meters and is a distinctive feature. The building also contains a collection of Jordanian contemporary art.",
